[- Reference: ast-bin. -]
[page id='ref-ast-bin'
  [meta
    title='ast-bin Binary AST'
    layout='reference'
    nav-order='460'
    audience='lookup'
    summary='Versioned binary serialization of the CXDM tree. Used for cross-binding handoff and stable disk storage.'
  ]

  [section id='what' title='Purpose'
    [prose ast-bin is a compact, versioned binary serialization of the CXDM tree. It round-trips byte-for-byte with the canonical text form, runs at the FFI boundary between every binding and libcx, and forms the canonical-bytes baseline for the cross-binding conformance suite.]
  ]

  [section id='version' title='Version'
    [prose v6 ships at v0.7.0; advertised by capability bit 29 on the libcx C ABI. Earlier versions (v3, v4, v5) remain readable by libcx through the lifetime of v0.7.x. Bindings query cx_features before writing v6 payloads to confirm support on the linked libcx.]
  ]

  [section id='cli' title='CLI'
    [code lang='shell' src='''cx --ast menu.cx > menu.ast.json
# binary form via the C ABI / per-binding API:
# cx_to_ast_bin   (encode)
# cx_from_ast_bin (decode)''']
  ]

  [section id='spec' title='Specification'
    [prose The wire format is documented in spec/ast_bin.md. Tag bytes 0x0F / 0x10 / 0x11 cover the ADR 0017 collection literals (Sequence / Array / Map). Body refs land at ast_bin v3; the v4-to-v6 increments cover schema-content-mismatch fields, validator metadata, and the typed-table compression added at v0.7.0.]
  ]

  [section id='related' title='Related'
    [list
      [item path='bindings/c-abi'      label='C ABI — the cx_to_ast_bin entry points']
      [item path='reference/data-bin'  label='data-bin — the columnar Arrow / Parquet binding']
    ]
  ]

  [preserve id='author-notes'
    [- Empty by default. -]
  ]
]
